Overlapping strcpy in the qualified-symbol scanner action (asm7090 2.3.2, scanner.h cases 3/12).

    iiicp = strchr(symbol, '$'); *iiicp = 0; iiicp++;
    strcpy (qualsym, symbol);
    strcpy (symbol, iiicp);        <- src and dst overlap: undefined behaviour

With glibc 2.36 on x86-64 the overlapping strcpy shifts the tail ("$ERROR" -> "EROOR",
"$ZERO" -> "ZROO", "$CONS" -> "CNSS"), so every $-prefixed cross-namespace reference in the
LISP 1.5 deck (741 of them) was looked up under a mangled name and reported undefined
(Techne, 2026-09-16, techne/fossils/specimens/lisp-1-5-ibm7090-1962). memmove is defined
for overlap. Applied to the WORLD (Dockerfile), never to a preserved body.

--- asm7090/scanner.h
+++ asm7090/scanner.h
@@ -86,2 +86,2 @@
 	 strcpy (qualsym, symbol);
-	 strcpy (symbol, iiicp);
+	 memmove (symbol, iiicp, strlen (iiicp) + 1);
